Composery updates own the whole update surface

Composery has exactly one update mechanism: the composery-updates builtin
extension (keyed on COMPOSERY_BUILD_VERSION, compared against
COMPOSERY_BUILD_SOURCE's GitHub releases on a self-hosted instance and against
the website's fleet release on a cloud instance; automatic on startup and manual via
the composery.checkForUpdates command). This patch owns everything around that:

- adds the File-menu "Check for Updates" item that fires the extension command
  (client.ts, MenubarHomeMenu).
- removes code-server's own update notifier remnants so no second mechanism
  survives: the client checkUpdates loop + its storage plumbing (client.ts),
  the updateEndpoint product field emission (webClientServer.ts) and its
  interface field (product.ts), the disable-update-check server arg
  (serverEnvironmentService.ts), plus the server side: the /update route and
  UpdateProvider (patch-deleted files) and the disable-update-check CLI flag.

